From aabedf401d8d53e1b79757029d71f9ecc925c809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:07:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(Input Layers): emit events when a layer activation
 deactivates

A `layer` target event can now carry `on_deactivation`: events to emit,
each as a press followed by a release, when its activator deactivates
the layer (a hold input released, a toggle input pressed again). With
`only_when_unused: true` they go out only if none of the layer's mappings
produced an output while it was active:

    - layer:
        name: mouse_mode
        on_deactivation:
          only_when_unused: true
          emit_events:
            - gamepad: { button: Guide }

One button can then open a layer when held with others and keep its own
meaning when tapped alone. Clearing the layer stack (profile change,
removed source device, suspend) emits nothing, and `layer` events in
`emit_events` are ignored with a warning.
